      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: support GCP broker metadata auth",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- allow the GCP broker provider to use the Google metadata server when `CRABBOX_GCP_CREDENTIAL_SOURCE=metadata` is set\n- keep service-account-key auth working by default when both `GCP_CLIENT_EMAIL` and `GCP_PRIVATE_KEY` are configured\n- fail clearly for partial key-pair config or keyless config without the explicit metadata credential source\n- update GCP provider readiness and brokered auth docs for metadata-server / Workload Identity deployments\n- add Worker regression tests for metadata auth and GCP readiness\n\nRefs https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/1016\n\n## Config and secret implications\n\nGoogle-hosted coordinators can use the attached service account identity by setting `CRABBOX_GCP_CREDENTIAL_SOURCE=metadata` plus `GCP_PROJECT_ID` or `CRABBOX_GCP_PROJECT`. Portable coordinators keep using `GCP_CLIENT_EMAIL` and `GCP_PRIVATE_KEY`; if either key variable is set, both must be set. Project-only GCP config remains not configured unless the metadata credential source is explicitly selected.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm test -- --run test/gcp.test.ts test/fleet.test.ts`\n- `npm run format:check`\n- `npm run lint`\n- `npm run check`\n- `npm run check:node`\n- `GOPATH=/tmp/go-path-crabbox GOMODCACHE=/tmp/go-mod-cache-crabbox GOCACHE=/tmp/go-cache-crabbox scripts/check-docs.sh`\n- `npm test`\n- `HOME=/tmp/crabbox-home npm run build`\n- `npm run build:node`\n\nInternal tracking: ref REI-2531",
